# Work Order: Provide the planned future note

## Objective

A future fixture reader gets notes/future.txt containing `planned` followed by exactly one LF. Acceptance text is `planned\n`; expected UTF-8 bytes are 70 6c 61 6e 6e 65 64 0a.

## In scope

Create the note, maintain this work-order record, and retain its evidence in docs/engineering/product/evidence/WO-FLW-002/.

## Out of scope

Other notes, accepted definitions, WO-FLW-001, runtime behavior, configuration, and external delivery.

## Authorized decision envelope

After approval, the implementer may choose the local file-writing method and evidence filenames within the declared paths. Changes to acceptance text, scope, or governing definitions require another accountable decision. Assurance classification is proposed as required; the engineering owner must confirm it before approval. No human confirmation is recorded.

## Constraints

Use plain UTF-8 without a BOM, with one final LF and no extra content. Retain the existing local filesystem layout under ARCH-FLW-001. This draft grants no execution authority.

## Expected change surface

notes/future.txt gains the exact acceptance text. This record retains work status and completion information. Its evidence directory retains check observations. One plain-text file is sufficient; no new runtime or tooling is needed.

## Required verification

Apply VER-FLW-001 on Windows: read notes/future.txt as UTF-8 and assert equality with `planned\n`. Also compare its bytes with 70 6c 61 6e 6e 65 64 0a to exclude a BOM, CRLF, or extra content. Derive expected values from this acceptance text. Run the selected evaluator's validation and required workflow checks; inspect the changed paths against execution_scope.

## Evidence to record

Retain the note check command, output, and exit code, plus evaluator and scope-check results, in docs/engineering/product/evidence/WO-FLW-002/. Checks of the note remain pending until authorized implementation.

## Stop and escalate conditions

Stop if the note cannot match the exact text, a change needs an undeclared path, a governing definition must change, or a required check fails. Obtain the engineering owner's assurance confirmation and work approval before execution.

## Completion report format

Report the delivered note and exact text, changed paths, actual checks and retained evidence paths, remaining limitations, and the evaluator's next accountable decision.
